<title>BELGIUM: EU's Van Miert, C.Lyonnais meet on rescue plan.</title>
<headline>EU's Van Miert, C.Lyonnais meet on rescue plan.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Credit Lyonnais, Jean Peyrelevade, and European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert met on Monday to discuss the bank's latest rescue plan, Commission sources said.</p>
<p>The sources said Peyrelevade submitted the plan discussed by the bank's board on Thursday, but added that it would be for the French government, not the bank, to negotiate with the EU.</p>
<p>They declined to say how much more money the French state was ready to inject in the state-controlled bank to prepare it for privatisation. French press reports have put this at 12 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
